B.LB=new A.bF(35,"pass\xe9 compos\xe9 with \xeatre","A2","Some movement/change verbs and pronominal verbs use \xeatre; participle agrees with subject.","present of `\xeatre` + past participle (+agreement)",B.X7,"Common \xeatre verbs: aller, venir, arriver, partir, entrer, sortir, na\xeetre, mourir, rester, tomber.","Same pass\xe9 compos\xe9 idea, but the auxiliary is `\xeatre`, so the past participle agrees with the subject.","Use `\xeatre` with many verbs of movement/change of state and with pronominal verbs. The learner's job is to conjugate `\xeatre` first, then adjust the participle ending: add `e` for feminine, `s` for plural, `es` for feminine plural.",B.S_,B.SN,"The auxiliary is the part you conjugate. The past participle is not `arrive`; it is `arriv\xe9`, then agreement is added when needed.")
