B.Lx=new A.bF(41,"il faut (obligation)","A2","il faut + infinitive expresses general obligation or necessity.","`il faut + infinitive`; negative: `il ne faut pas + infinitive`",B.XR,"il faut is impersonal. Use devoir for a specific person: Je dois partir.","`Il faut` gives a general rule or need, like `it is necessary to...`.","The form `faut` does not change with the person. Use it when the instruction applies generally. Use `devoir` when you want to say exactly who must do something.",B.a08,B.Px,"Do not conjugate the second verb after `il faut`: `il faut r\xe9server`, not `il faut r\xe9serves`.")
