B.Lv=new A.bF(47,"Expanded Negation","A2","French has several negative pairs beyond ne\u2026pas.","`ne\u2026 jamais`, `ne\u2026 plus`, `ne\u2026 rien`, `ne\u2026 personne`, `ne\u2026 que`",B.a3i,"ne\u2026 que means only, not a true negative.","These are negative pairs: one part before the verb, one part after it.","The first part is usually `ne/n'` before the conjugated verb. The second part gives the meaning: never, no longer, nothing, nobody, or only.",B.a2I,B.a_x,"`Ne... que` means `only`, so it is restrictive rather than truly negative.")
