B.KY=new A.bF(49,"pass\xe9 compos\xe9 vs. imparfait","A2","pass\xe9 compos\xe9 for completed events; imparfait for background/habits.","background in imparfait + event in pass\xe9 compos\xe9",B.WY,"Time markers help: hier/soudain \u2192 events; avant/tous les jours \u2192 background.","Use imperfect for the scene; use pass\xe9 compos\xe9 for the event that happens in the scene.","Imagine a story timeline. The imperfect paints the background or repeated habit. The pass\xe9 compos\xe9 marks completed actions that move the story forward.",B.W6,B.Ug,"The same English past form can translate two ways. `I watched TV` can be `je regardais` for background or `j'ai regard\xe9` for one finished event.")
